# Where the ai-devkit finds the material it reads.
#
# Copy this file to the project root as aidk-config.env. Every setting below
# is commented out and shows its default, so the copy changes nothing until a
# line is uncommented: remove the # from the one to change, and change it.
#
# One KEY=value per line. The file is read, never run: no quotes, no export,
# no $VARIABLES. A plain path is read from the project root, one beginning
# with / is taken as written, and {ai-devkit} is where the kit itself sits.
# A path set here must exist.

# AIDK_RULES={ai-devkit}/presets/rules
# AIDK_CONVENTIONS=aidk-conventions
# AIDK_PLANS=aidk-plans
# AIDK_REVIEW=aidk-review
# AIDK_ORGANIZER=aidk-organizer

# The command that hands out a clean copy of the pushed work, for checking
# a red no step explains. Its default names no file: no copy is taken, and
# such a red is reported as it stands.
# AIDK_CLEAN_COPY=aidk-clean-copy
